WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.286
CPython and PyPy run the same Python program.

00:00:03.286 --> 00:00:07.521
PyPy can speed up a long loop after its compiler warms up.

00:00:07.521 --> 00:00:12.560
Compare both on representative inputs when the contest supports them.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:17.451
Splitting a buffer turns whitespace-separated input into tokens.

00:00:17.451 --> 00:00:22.002
Bulk reading is convenient, but holds the whole input in memory.

00:00:22.002 --> 00:00:25.060
Read a line at a time if the file is large.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:30.404
A thousand items scanned a thousand times means a million visits.

00:00:30.404 --> 00:00:34.638
Changing interpreters cannot remove that repeated work.

00:00:34.638 --> 00:00:37.640
First look for a way to reuse a result.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.472
Removing the first item of a list shifts the rest.

00:00:41.472 --> 00:00:45.360
A deque supports removal at either end in constant time.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:49.040
Choose the structure around the operation you repeat.
